WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:04.565
Stage twenty-five: your AI, your plan.

2
00:00:05.415 --> 00:00:10.124
Camille already pays for ChatGPT. Her plan is enough.

3
00:00:10.224 --> 00:00:20.074
ChatGPT Plus or Pro, or GitHub Copilot Pro, Pro plus, Business, Enterprise. The free offer is refused, and the coach says so.

4
00:00:20.924 --> 00:00:26.806
One install option: llm chatgpt, or llm copilot.

5
00:00:26.906 --> 00:00:31.892
Then you sign in once, yourself, in a terminal. Never in the background.

6
00:00:32.742 --> 00:00:40.629
The sign-in lives in a store dedicated to the coach, mode seven hundred. Your personal OpenCode is untouched.

7
00:00:40.729 --> 00:00:44.777
The counter shows no euros: “included in your plan”.

8
00:00:45.627 --> 00:00:53.664
The chat moves onto the plan. The sync is an explicit choice: yes on a fresh install, otherwise sync subscription.

9
00:00:53.764 --> 00:01:00.520
No official rule allows scheduled use of a consumer plan. No sync subscription forbids it.

10
00:01:01.370 --> 00:01:07.401
Claude plan at its limit? Change the AI of the sync alone, without touching the chat.

11
00:01:07.501 --> 00:01:15.751
One command: sync anthropic. Haiku five point five by default, paid per token. Back to claude subscription.

12
00:01:16.601 --> 00:01:23.294
The coach stopped answering? Test the connection: a button in the macOS app and on the chat page.

13
00:01:23.394 --> 00:01:28.849
Or check in the terminal, offline; with probe, one minimal call per provider.

14
00:01:29.699 --> 00:01:35.880
Token expired? Chat and test use the same words; the sync sends a notification.

15
00:01:35.980 --> 00:01:40.838
The message gives the command. The coach never signs in on its own.

16
00:01:43.388 --> 00:01:48.161
To go further: the “Choosing your AI” page of the documentation.
